          "title": "You'll want to know: ஆனந்தம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆனந்தம் — āṉantam — \"bliss; great joy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பேரனைப் பார்த்ததும் தாத்தாவுக்கு ஆனந்தம். pēraṉaip pārttatum tāttāvukku āṉantam. Grandfather was overjoyed to see his grandson."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆனந்தக் கண்ணீர், tears of joy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆனந்தம் (āṉantam) is borrowed from Sanskrit ānanda, \"happiness\" (CDIAL 1172), with the Tamil ending -அம்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
